        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 18:56:05.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 04:17:38.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lod: keep MDT pool members apart from OSTs",
        "message": "LU-21061 lod: keep MDT pool members apart from OSTs\n\nA pool can only list OSTs.  lod_pool_add() looks the target up in\nlod_ost_descs only, and every OST allocation path reads pool_obds,\nso an MDT index there would be taken for an OST index.\n\nKeep MDT members in a separate pool_mdts list, and the local MDT,\nwhich has no lod_mdt_descs entry, in pool_local_mdt.  Choose the\nlist from the target name in lod_pool_add() and lod_pool_remove(),\nand list MDT members after the OSTs in lod.*.pools.<pool>.\n\nThe MGS still refuses MDT names, so nothing changes for users yet.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: Icbc149a898e44bbf9e0e35173ba39ba03a1735f4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
